1
00:00:00,481 --> 00:00:03,011
(Leonard:)...so we came up with
kind of a cool solution.

2
00:00:03,651 --> 00:00:04,811
Oh, yeah? What's that?

3
00:00:04,986 --> 00:00:06,216
(Sheldon:)It's simple, really.

4
00:00:06,387 --> 00:00:09,477
(Sheldon:)It occurred to me that
knowing and not knowing...

5
00:00:09,657 --> 00:00:14,687
(Sheldon:)...can be achieved by creating a macroscopic
example of quantum superposition...

6
00:00:14,863 --> 00:00:20,863
(Sheldon:)...the principle that a physical system exists
partially in all its possible states at once.

7
00:00:21,035 --> 00:00:22,905
(Penny:)We were all thinking it, really.

8
00:00:25,506 --> 00:00:27,836
(Penny:)It was kind of the elephant
in the room, so...

9
00:00:29,944 --> 00:00:33,934
(Sheldon:)Anyway, um, I realized
if we each present you...

10
00:00:34,115 --> 00:00:36,605
(Sheldon:)...with an account of
what your father wrote to you...

11
00:00:36,784 --> 00:00:40,724
(Sheldon:)...only one of which is true,
and we don't tell you which one it is...

12
00:00:40,889 --> 00:00:45,049
(Sheldon:)...you will forever be
in a state of epistemic ambivalence.

13
00:00:45,226 --> 00:00:48,956
(Penny:)Yeah, and I said if it wasn't epistemic,
we might as well not do it.

14
00:00:51,933 --> 00:00:53,733
(Bernadette:)Sit down, honey.

15
00:00:54,669 --> 00:00:58,019
- Raj, you're up.
- Okay, um, ahem.

